@startuml
title Sequence diagram: send an event for a safety check
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API and PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the
' draw.io and PDF versions.
' A notification is a record saved in PostgreSQL. Nothing is pushed to its recipient
' (no email, websocket or polling): the Web App fetches it later with
' GET /api/notifications, as the second section shows.

actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
actor "Safety\nOfficer" as safety
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Send an Approved event to Safety Review (its venues and equipment must be settled) ==
coordinator -> web : Send for safety check
autonumber
web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/safety-review
api -> db : Status becomes safety_review
api -> db : Save notification:\nall Safety Officers
api --> web : The request, now in Safety Review
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the request

== Later, the Web App fetches the Safety Officers' saved notifications (nothing is pushed) ==
safety -> web : Open notifications
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/notifications
api --> web : An event is waiting for your safety review
autonumber stop
web --> safety : Show notifications

== Safety Officer opens the events in Safety Review ==
safety -> web : Open the list
autonumber resume
web -> api : GET /api/events/requests/awaiting-safety-review
api --> web : Events in Safety Review, soonest first
autonumber stop
web --> safety : Show the events
@enduml
